ese combinations use my bomb with extras. Wasteful at this stage.\n\n**Best Move: Pair ♥K ♣K**\n\nThis forces high responses (Aces or 2s) while preserving my triple 2s bomb. If the landlord uses their last A or 2 to beat this, it weakens their endgame. If they pass, my teammate might take control. This play reduces my hand efficiently while keeping my bomb intact for emergency blocking.\n\nReason:\nPlaying the pair of Kings applies pressure by forcing high cards (Aces or 2s) to respond, while preserving my triple 2s bomb for critical defensive moments. With the landlord at only 4 cards, I need to maintain my strongest control card (the bomb) to potentially block their final plays. This balanced approach reduces my hand count while keeping maximum defensive capability.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥K", "♣K"]}'}
